  "notes": "{匂|にお}う is intransitive (⟦{自動詞|じどうし}→自動詞：10977_jidoushi⟧). There is no common transitive pair.\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{匂|にお}って⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ indicates an ongoing state of smelling or giving off an odor.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦いい→いい：00118_ii⟧⟦{匂|にお}い→匂い：00874_nioi⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{匂|にお}う (to smell nice)\n- ⟦{変|へん}な→変：01124_hen⟧⟦{匂|にお}い→匂い：00874_nioi⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{匂|にお}う (to smell strange)\n- ⟦{犯罪|はんざい}→犯罪：03569_hanzai⟧⟦の→の：09472_no⟧⟦{匂|にお}い→匂い：00874_nioi⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{匂|にお}う (to smack of crime)\n- ～⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{匂|にお}う: What is giving off the smell\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{臭|くさ}い→臭い：01133_kusai⟧: Adjective meaning \"smelly/stinky\" (negative)\n- ⟦{香|かお}る→香る：14841_kaoru⟧: More literary, typically positive fragrance\n- ⟦{匂|にお}い→匂い：00874_nioi⟧: Noun form meaning \"smell/scent\"\n\nThe kanji {匂} is used for general smells, while {臭} specifically refers to bad odors.",
